docs(backlog): record the requirement to split a very large initial requirement into sequenced epics

PO ruling 2026-11-19 (candidate 32 session): a very large initial requirement package should not be handled as one PRD and one Spec reopened for every later epic. The item records the wish for the 0.7.1 window (Nightwing): the Pipeline proposes a split into separate blocks with the user, makes one continuous architecture analysis of the whole package first, gives each block its own PRD, Spec and slices under that shared architecture, works one block at a time, and records any later change of the shared modules as an amendment. It is a requirement for later, not part of 0.7.0, and names its open design questions; the first step would be an ADR.

